From 6e18d7e974e3f29fb28eab7ade3c34a699395325 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 05:13:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 398/638] [AROS] Trace compositor sink instances before Mojo

Runtime 40 proves the browser root embeds one child Surface while Viz receives no child frame. Replace the process-global frame counter with bounded per-instance telemetry and record sink construction, pipe type, binding/connection state, LocalSurfaceId assignment, begin-frame demand/delivery, no-frame acknowledgements, submissions, and disconnects.

The AROS-only probe distinguishes a child sink that is never created or scheduled from one that submits into a bound Mojo remote but fails before Viz dispatch.

AI_PHASE: chromium-process-model

AI_STATUS: diagnostic

AI_OBSERVED: Root SurfaceContent reference reaches Viz, but zero non-root CompositorFrameSinkSupport submissions arrive.

AI_FIX_REASON: Move observability to each AsyncLayerTreeFrameSink instance before the Mojo submission boundary.

AI_SCOPE: cc/mojo_embedder/async_layer_tree_frame_sink.cc and .h only.

AI_VALIDATION: git diff --check; build and hosted runtime pending by design.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: runtime40 root/child discriminator -> per-instance renderer sink lifecycle -> transport receiver boundary.
---
 .../async_layer_tree_frame_sink.cc            | 98 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../async_layer_tree_frame_sink.h             |  7 ++
 2 files changed, 100 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

